CloudBurrow patch 92 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1767).

A load job's destination table, and a query job's, can be in another
project than the job's (BigQuery: "the destination table can be in a
different project"). The emulator looked the destination's dataset up in
the job's project: it answered a load into `other.ds.t` 404 dataset "ds"
is not found, and a query whose destinationTable is `other.ds.q` "failed
to find destination dataset: ds". Both now look the dataset up, and make
a table that does not exist, in the table's own project (one the
emulator has; 404 "project P is not found" otherwise); the rows were
already written by the table reference's project.

cloudburrow_load_other_project_test.go (TestLoadIntoAnotherProjectsTable):
two CSV loads of a job of project test into other.ds.t, a new table then
WRITE_APPEND, write the other project's table and none in test, and a
query of test's job with destination other.ds.q writes it. It fails
without the patch.

